<programme start="20261110120000 +0000" stop="20261110150000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Florida State at Boston College</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Florida State Seminoles (3-5) face the Boston College Eagles (4-4) at Alumni Stadium for an ACC match. Florida State seeks to snap a three-game skid after a 36-24 defeat to Clemson, while Boston College looks to rebound from a 47-2 loss to Duke.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261110150000 +0000" stop="20261110160000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">ACC Network Football Podcast</title><desc lang="en">This podcast covers all things ACC football. Hosted by first round NFL Draft pick and former Florida State quarterback EJ Manuel and former Georgia Tech running back Roddy Jones.</desc><credits><actor>EJ Manuel</actor><actor>Roddy Jones</actor></credits><category lang="en">News</category><category lang="en">Sports</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p30993883_b_v11_aa.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261110160000 +0000" stop="20261110190000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Merrimack at Wake Forest</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Warriors (4-5) visit the No. 16 Demon Deacons at Allegacy Federal Credit Union Stadium. The Warriors seek to make it three straight after beating the Seahawks 19-14. The Demon Deacons seek to make it six straight after beating the Cavaliers 51-7.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261110190000 +0000" stop="20261110220000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Virginia Tech at SMU</sub-title><desc lang="en">The SMU Mustangs (6-2) host the Virginia Tech Hokies (6-2) at Gerald J. Ford Stadium in an ACC matchup. Virginia Tech seeks its third straight win after beating Clemson 20-16, while SMU fell to Syracuse 30-27 and relies on quarterback Kevin Jennings.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
